course: dictionary
lesson: 10113
title: The number thirty
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Thirty is the number 30. It is three tens: ten, twenty, thirty. You can count in tens to reach it, and each jump of ten gets you one step closer.
explain: Thirty also shows up in time. Half an hour is 30 minutes, so «half past» on a clock means thirty minutes past the hour. The short hand points halfway between two numbers, and the long hand points to the 6.
explain: Words around a number give clues to its meaning. «EVERYONE in my class has got them» usually means a few children, perhaps four out of thirty, not the whole class. The fair question to ask is: who exactly?
fact: Thirty means 30, which is three tens.
fact: Half an hour is 30 minutes.
fact: The rhyme says «Thirty days hath September, April, June and November». Here "hath" is old English for "has".
fact: In 1862 Charles Darwin predicted that an orchid with a tube about thirty centimetres long would have a moth with a tongue that long. It was found after his death and named praedicta, meaning predicted.
exercise: How many tens make thirty? | 1 | 10 | 2 | *3
exercise: How many minutes are in half an hour? | *30 | 45 | 15 | 60
exercise: The rhyme says «Thirty days hath September». How many days does September have? | 28 | *30 | 29 | 31
test: What time does «half past» on a clock mean? | 45 minutes past the hour | 60 minutes past the hour | *30 minutes past the hour | 15 minutes past the hour
test: Which number is three tens? | 300 | *30 | 3 | 13
exam: Max has thirty sweets and shares them equally between 3 friends. How many sweets does each friend get? | 5 | 3 | *10 | 30
